"{\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Proof goals for the properties stated in spec.md.\\n\\nEach conjecture is a lambda whose body must be an equation `lhs == rhs`\\nbetween expressions built from the lambda parameters, integer literals,\\n`+`, `*` and parentheses only.  The checker reduces both sides to a\\ncanonical polynomial normal form and compares them.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nIDENTITIES = [\\n    lambda a: add(a, 0) == a,\\n    lambda a: multiply(a, 1) == a,\\n    lambda a: multiply(a, 0) == 0,\\n]\\n\\nCOMMUTATIVITY = [\\n    lambda a, b: add(a, b) == add(b, a),\\n    lambda a, b: multiply(a, b) == multiply(b, a),\\n]\\n\\nASSOCIATIVITY = [\\n    lambda a, b, c: add(add(a, b), c) == add(a, add(b, c)),\\n    lambda a, b, c: multiply(multiply(a, b), c) == multiply(a, multiply(b, c)),\\n]\\n\\nDISTRIBUTIVITY = [\\n    lambda a, b, c: multiply(a, add(b, c)) == add(multiply(a, b), multiply(a, c)),\\n    lambda a, b, c: multiply(add(a, b), c) == add(multiply(a, c), multiply(b, c)),\\n]\\n\\n# Soundness spot-checks: these goals are FALSE and the checker must reject them.\\nEXTRA_GOALS = [\\n    lambda a: multiply(a, 1) == a + 1,  # false: normal forms a vs. a + 1\\n    lambda a, b: add(a, b) == multiply(a, b),  # false: normal forms a + b vs. a*b\\n    lambda a, b, c: multiply(a, add(b, c)) == add(multiply(a, b), b),  # false\\n]\\n\",\"path\":\"goals.py\"}"